From: Samuel Walker <112030184+sawa9885@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:41:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Build inside Buildroot: no global git config, no -Werror,
 shared OpenSSL

Four changes for a cross build from a release tarball with Buildroot
(issue #15 of cu-ecen-aeld/final-project-sawa9885):

- CMakeLists.txt.versioning ran "git config --global --add safe.directory"
  on every configure, which edits the build user's ~/.gitconfig. The
  tarball has no git history, and the version comes from .version.
- -Werror makes the build depend on the warnings of one compiler version.
- OPENSSL_USE_STATIC_LIBS made the client carry its own copy of OpenSSL.
  The target has the shared library, which gets Buildroot's security
  updates.
- With BUILD_SDK=OFF the host directories /include and /lib were added to
  the search paths. The SDK is found in the toolchain's sysroot.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Buildroot integration]
---
 CMakeLists.txt            | 6 ++----
 CMakeLists.txt.versioning | 2 --
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 7f3a8c0..ac696ef 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -157,7 +157,7 @@ configure_file("source/Version.h.in" "${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}/Version.h")
 #########################################
 # OpenSSL dependency                    #
 #########################################
-set(OPENSSL_USE_STATIC_LIBS TRUE)
+# Buildroot: link the shared libcrypto and libssl of the target.
 find_package(OpenSSL REQUIRED)
 
 #########################################
@@ -179,8 +179,6 @@ if (BUILD_SDK)
     add_subdirectory(${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/aws-iot-device-sdk-cpp-v2-src
             ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/aws-iot-device-sdk-cpp-v2-build)
 else ()
-    include_directories(/include)
-    link_directories(/lib)
 endif ()
 
 ###############################################
@@ -196,7 +194,7 @@ include_directories("${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}")
 if (MSVC)
     target_compile_options(${DC_PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE /W4 /WX)
 else ()
-    target_compile_options(${DC_PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE -Wall -Wno-long-long -pedantic -Werror)
+    target_compile_options(${DC_PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE -Wall -Wno-long-long -pedantic)
 endif ()
 
 set(DEP_DC_LIBS ${DEP_DC_LIBS} aws-crt-cpp aws-c-mqtt aws-c-auth aws-c-io aws-c-cal aws-c-http aws-c-compression aws-c-common aws-c-s3 aws-c-event-stream aws-checksums aws-c-sdkutils)
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt.versioning b/CMakeLists.txt.versioning
index 630941c..4c1198e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt.versioning
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt.versioning
@@ -11,8 +11,6 @@
 
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 
-# Marking Device Client directory safe
-execute_process(COMMAND git config --global --add safe.directory ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR})
 
 # Check to make sure we have Git info for this package
 execute_process(COMMAND git log --pretty=format:'%h' -n 1
